commit 6be00ee984003683049389e4e089950e60f86aa4
Author: Burak Emre Kabakcı <emrekabakci@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 20 16:12:34 2026 +0100

    refactor(behaviors): rename public watcher_id -> behavior_id + steer telemetry (#2030)

    * fix(behaviors): rename public watcher_id->behavior_id in REST, proposal check, get_behavior I/O

    - rest-api: behavior_id query param + payload keys
    - agent-routes: pending-proposal target reads args.behavior_id
    - get_behavior + WatcherWindow/WatcherMetadata schemas: emit behavior_id
    - DB columns unchanged (watchers.id stays internal)

    * feat(steer): tag steer telemetry with behavior source + active_run policy

    Enrich the 'Message steered into active agent turn' log with steerSource
    (behavior|human), behaviorId, and behaviorActiveRunPolicy so real usage of
    active_run:steer can be measured before deciding whether to keep the knob.

    * test(behaviors): update fixtures to behavior_id public field

    * chore(behaviors): regen client types + SDK doc examples for behavior_id

    - types.gen.ts: manage_behaviors/get_behavior I/O -> behavior_id (kept number-typed
      watcher_source/get_content/manage_classifiers fields as watcher_id)
    - method-metadata: client.behaviors.* examples use behavior_id; window output
      ctx.window.behavior_id; watcher_source provenance key unchanged

    * fix(behaviors): migrate CLI apply to behavior_id + fix installed ids & reaction example

    - CLI apply/init-from-org talk to /manage_behaviors and /behaviors over
      the wire; migrate their payloads, REST query param, response reads, and
      RemoteBehavior type from watcher_id/watcher_ids to behavior_id/behavior_ids
      so 'lobu apply' keeps working against the renamed public contract.
    - catalog/installed.ts: read behavior_id from handleList rows so installed
      Behavior resource ids are no longer empty strings.
    - method-metadata.ts: notifications.send example uses ctx.window.watcher_id
      (ReactionContext.window exposes watcher_id, not behavior_id; watcher_source
      was intentionally not renamed).

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

    * test(behaviors): update stale watcher_id expectations to behavior_id

    The public rename now emits behavior_id/behavior_ids, but two unit suites
    still asserted the old watcher_id contract:
    - sdk-search: behaviors.get/trigger drill-down expected watcher_id and
      behaviors.delete expected watcher_ids; updated to behavior_id/behavior_ids.
    - watcher-execution-config: manage_behaviors update helper passed watcher_id,
      now rejected as an unknown argument; switched to behavior_id.

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

    * test(behaviors): update sdk-e2e to behavior_id for manage_behaviors

    The public rename renders the manage_behaviors list output as behavior_id
    and makes behavior_id the input arg for trigger/complete_window (the strict
    schema now rejects watcher_id). The e2e script still read watcher_id from the
    list (so it never found the digest Behavior) and passed watcher_id to
    trigger/complete_window. Read behavior_id from the list and send behavior_id
    to those actions. read_knowledge (get_content) keeps watcher_id since that
    tool was intentionally not renamed.

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

    * test(behaviors): migrate integration/e2e fixtures to behavior_id args + response assertions

    Fixes the ~25 integration suites failing in CI (automation-contract, watchers-crud,
    promote-keyed-entities, group-edit, manual-trigger, feedback-contract, event-activation,
    manage-behaviors-*, etc). Only manage_behaviors/get_behavior ARG keys + RESPONSE reads
    renamed; SQL columns, event/reaction metadata, and other tools' watcher_id left unchanged.

    * ci: trigger full run on behavior_id fixtures

    * test(behaviors): migrate all-tools-e2e + classifiers-isolation fixtures to behavior_id

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

    * test(behaviors): migrate main's cross-org delete test to behavior_id public field

    Reconciles the BUG C delete-isolation test added on main (#2013) with this
    PR's public watcher_id -> behavior_id rename: the behaviors.create response and
    behaviors.delete argument now use behavior_id/behavior_ids. The raw watchers SQL
    (WHERE id = ...) stays on the DB column.

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

    * fix(behaviors): stringify behavior_id in get_behavior window + metadata results

    The watchers.id column comes back from postgres.js as a raw integer, but
    WatcherWindowSchema/WatcherMetadataSchema type behavior_id as Type.String(),
    so the structuredContent validation fails downstream (same pattern list.ts
    already guards). Coerce both result sites with String().

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

    * fix(behaviors): read behavior_id in MCP markdown formatter

    The watcher_id→behavior_id rename updated handlers (crud.ts, get_behavior.ts)
    and SDK/CLI/tests but missed the default MCP markdown formatter. Result
    objects now emit behavior_id, so the formatter rendered 'Behavior ID: undefined'
    and the create-with-template branch (checking !result.watcher_id) misfired for
    every create. read_knowledge's own param stays watcher_id (unchanged tool
    contract), so its example label is preserved; only the value source
    (behavior.behavior_id) and the manage_behaviors result reads change.

    Found by pi-review (bug_free 34, 1 blocker).

    ---------

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

